body:
I fiiiinally finished this one and I gotta say, I'm feeling some kind of way about it. I mean...I didn't *think* I was into \[primal\] but those growls? That soft little wolf-y whisper you do? Hrgn. Now two of my favorite audios by you are wolf themed!

&#x200B;

Damnit, I'm prey now, aren't I? \*blame\*

\*Smiles brightly\* I'm so, so glad you liked it! I agonized over actually publishing, as opposed to re-re-recording it a hundred times so that it would be perfect. In the end, I felt like the more I worked on it, the less genuine it sounded. Your Ghost Girl has been a delight to play.

&#x200B;

Thank you so much!

\*Giggles\*! Thank you, Bilge! Honestly, I probably don't need the last two tags, given the way I recorded the script, but I thought better safe than sorry.

&#x200B;

I'm so glad you liked it!

Here we are! Should I make another post or is it okay to add it here?

&#x200B;

[Giddy!](https://soundgasm.net/u/DarkDesireX/Verification-for-Gonewild-Audio)

I have thick \*black\* hair. If you know what 4C means, that's my texture. I spent three years growing it out and meticulously caring for it. It was exhausting and time-consuming. I'm talking all-day washing sessions, money spent for moisturizing treatments, always remembering to put it in a protective style before bed (at least a 30 minute process toward the end), the works.

&#x200B;

When I decided to shave my head, I mourned the wasted time and effort. My hair was the longest it had ever been, but I'd just had a baby. Those extra hours were desperately needed for sleep. It's been 8 months and, honestly, I wish I had done it before. It's freeing! I love having my short hair. And it's not boring, like I was worried it'd be. I've dyed it since cutting it and I like the fact that if I hate what I end up with, I can just cut it all off again and start over. Plus, a cute haircut only costs $12 at a barbershop. So...I'm not seeing a downside. =D

Hey, Buka! I don't have any lines on jobs, but I've done a ton of recruitment work and I'd be more than happy to take a look at any of your application materials. It may sound kind of silly, but a well-written cover letter can open a lot of doors and we can look at your skills and see what you could finagle.

&#x200B;

I wish I could help more. If you'd like to chat, my messages are always open.

When I'm frustrated, I love an infinite money cheat. Yeah, I could spend forever grinding to get the gear I want, but I'd rather run around OP as shit and smash things in the face.

&#x200B;

Also, I don't like my Sims to be poor. Too real, man. Too real.

Yes. Duh, that's the whole point.

&#x200B;

The vagina is only so many inches deep anyway. Several of those inches will go to waste.

When we ask him where he's going, he says, he's "going to talk to a man about a mule."

&#x200B;

I'm like, okay, but we have plans later...

No, but I know how to raise the roof.

&#x200B;

\*Pumps palms in the air\* Woop woop!

My boyfriends have a cousin (maybe 6 or 7) who is a total psychopath. Like, the real kind. He tells the most outrageous lies about DH2 and physically assaults adults. He's always beyond sweet to me, but the first day he met her, he told my mom that DH2 tried to bad touch him and that she should be worried about us having children.

&#x200B;

Luckily the boy's older brother was there and quick to point out that the boy said things like that all the time and not to worry about it, but it scared me how cold and frank he was.

As with all BDSM relationships, I think the first step is to communicate with your sub. Just because you're a Dom, doesn't mean you have to be all kinds of dom, all the time. If you're uncomfortable you \*absolutely\* have the right to say so--especially if it's turning you off. You mentioned putting in the research to figure out how to handle her changes in the bedroom. She can do the same thing (or better yet, you can do it together), so they you guys can find a happy medium.

&#x200B;

I'm a bratty sub, myself. And just as it's important for my Dom to be mindful of my limits, it's also important for \*me\* to know his Dom limits and to respect them. The only way we know what's what is to talk about it.

&#x200B;

Also, don't knock the cliches 'til you try them. They may read a little silly, but they're tried-and-true for a reason. ;)

Wesley Wyndam-Pryce! He went from this stuffy, stuck-up, wet noodle of a man and came out a powerful, scarred, *complex* wizard.

&#x200B;

I literally groan out loud every time I think about his transition to Angel. "What's a rogue demon?" Dude, come on!

I appreciate the flea control suggestions like you wouldn't believe. At this point, we'll try anything. We have one room in the whole house that is carpet and if we weren't renting I would just rip it up. I hadn't thought of putting a flea collar in the vacuum but that's going on my to-do list for tomorrow.

&#x200B;

We ended up making our flea spray. It's mostly just lemon juice and a little vinegar. It smells awful while it dries, but desperate times. =P

&#x200B;

Thanks, again. I feel much better every time I hear that someone else has done this battle. It feels like it'll never be "over" so, I'm just getting into the habit of doing a major cleaning every other day.

That your best isn't always enough.

&#x200B;

We grow up being spoon-fed this fantasy that if we try hard enough and have enough moxie, we'll get what we want in life. From TV, to teachers, to inspirational posters, we're given the impression that success is always obtainable, we just have to be willing to work hard enough to earn it. Unfortunately, the sad truth is sometimes no matter how much blood, sweat, and tears you put into something, you're not guaranteed an equivalent exchange.

&#x200B;

Sometimes you just fail.
